# Jenkins ML Pipeline - Required Steps

This file contains the main steps needed to set up, run, and validate the machine learning pipeline for the Water Potability project.

## 1) Set up the environment

From the project root:

```bash
cd /workspaces/Jenkins_Test
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -U pip
pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn fastapi uvicorn pydantic
```

If the repository already has a virtual environment configured, you can use:

```bash
cd /workspaces/Jenkins_Test
source .venv/bin/activate
```

## 2) Initialize DVC

```bash
dvc init
```

## 3) Define the pipeline stages

### Stage 1: Data Collection

```bash
dvc stage add -n Data_Collection \
  -d src/data_collection.py \
  -o data/raw \
  python src/data_collection.py
```

### Stage 2: Data Preprocessing

```bash
dvc stage add -n Data_Preprocessing \
  -d src/data_preprocessing.py \
  -o data/processed \
  python src/data_preprocessing.py
```

### Stage 3: Model Training

```bash
dvc stage add -n Model_Training \
  -d src/model_training.py \
  -o model.pkl \
  python src/model_training.py
```

### Stage 4: Model Evaluation

```bash
dvc stage add -n Evaluation \
  -d src/model_evaluation.py \
  -d model.pkl \
  -d data/processed/test_processed.csv \
  -o metrics.json \
  python src/model_evaluation.py
```

## 4) Run the pipeline

```bash
dvc dag
dvc repro
```

This will execute the pipeline stages in order and regenerate any required output files.

## 5) Run the FastAPI app

From the project root:

```bash
cd /workspaces/Jenkins_Test
.venv/bin/uvicorn src.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
```

Then test the app in a browser:

- Home: http://localhost:8000/
- API docs: http://localhost:8000/docs
- Prediction endpoint: http://localhost:8000/predict

## 6) Example prediction request

```bash
curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/predict" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "ph": 7.0,
    "Hardness": 200.0,
    "Solids": 20000.0,
    "Chloramines": 7.0,
    "Sulfate": 300.0,
    "Conductivity": 450.0,
    "Organic_carbon": 15.0,
    "Trihalomethanes": 60.0,
    "Turbidity": 3.5
  }'
```

## 7) Important notes

- Keep the virtual environment activated when running scripts.
- Make sure `model.pkl` exists before starting the API.
- Always run the data pipeline before model training and evaluation.
- Use the FastAPI /docs page to check all available routes without manual curl requests.
